Subject: [PATCH 10718/11362] Fifth data-marker instance, plus a second and
 distinct defect that must not be conflated

exp6865 is instance 5 and the first POSITIVE verdict quarantined by the data-borne
marker defect. Verdict complete_positive_v601_evidence_method_change_contract_ready,
substrate deterministic CPU read-only evidence reduction, 6.4s, stamped 03:36Z.
Markers appear as data keys -- "artifact_field": "model.unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF"
-- and in no declaration field. The four earlier instances were all complete_null.

A timing note is recorded with it because it nearly became a wrong finding: at 03:35Z
this artifact read CRITICAL-but-unstamped, which looks like the fabrication gate
missing one. It was not. The post-task verify had not run; the stamp landed a minute
later. An unstamped CRITICAL within a few minutes of an artifact's mtime is pending,
not skipped.

exp6866 is a DIFFERENT defect and the entry separates them explicitly. Substrate
native_gguf_tokenization_without_inference, 51.7s, stamped. Its markers are real --
the artifact genuinely loads the GGUF -- but the work is tokenization, not inference,
so plausible work falls under a 60s floor calibrated for full generation. That is a
miscalibrated floor, not a false positive, and a fix aimed at the marker scan would
not touch it.

The apparent inconsistency of exp6863 passing at 38.4s while exp6866 failed at 51.7s
resolves cleanly: duration_floor_for_artifact returns None for exp6863 because its
verdict is complete_blocked_* and blocked artifacts are exempt. The rule is
consistent; only the floor value is wrong for tokenization.

The fix has precedent rather than being invented here. live_llm_embedding_extraction
was added to the taxonomy on 2026-07-03 for the same shape -- a real GGUF load doing
something far cheaper than generation -- with its own 2.0s floor. That is a
documented taxonomy addition with a measured exemplar, not the forbidden practice of
adding a name to make a commit pass. It still needs the measurement of how long a 27B
tokenizer load actually takes before a number is chosen. Filed, not built.

